#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:28
#, no-c-format
msgid "Window Specific Settings"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:30
#, no-c-format
msgid "Here you can constomize window settings specifically only for some windows."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:34
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Please note that this configuration will not take effect if you do not use "
"&kwin; as your window manager. If you do use a different window manager, please "
"refer to its documentation for how to customize window behavior."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:40
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Many of the settings you can configure here are those you can configure on a "
"global basis in the <guilabel>Window Behavior</guilabel> "
"&kcontrol; module, however some of them are even more detailed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:44
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"They encompass geometry, placement, whether a window should be kept above or "
"below others, focus stealing prevention, and translucency settings."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:48
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can access this module in two ways: from the titlebar of the application "
"you wish to configure, or from &kcontrol;. If you start it from within "
"&kcontrol; you can use the <guibutton>New...</guibutton> "
"to create a window profile, and the <guibutton>Detect</guibutton> "
"button on the resulting dialog to partially fill in the required information "
"for the application you wish to configure."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:56
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can also at any time <guibutton>Modify...</guibutton> or <guibutton>"
"Delete</guibutton> any stored settings profile, and reorder the list. "
"Reordering the list is a convenience to help you sort the profiles, and has no "
"effect on how they are applied."
msgstr ""

